-- title:
--   Regularity of the two-chart model at the cusp ∞
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ be an integer and $p$ a prime. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $K\subseteq L((q))$ be the intermediate field `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull M)`, i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the image under the coefficientwise map `coeffEmb L` of the subfield of $\mathbf{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbf{Q}$ by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,d\,(jq)$ for the nonzero divisors $d\mid M$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $p$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion `coeffEmb L jq`. Put $B=\,$`chartAlgInf A K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, and let $\mathfrak n\subseteq B$ be a prime ideal characterised by: $b\in\mathfrak n$ if and only if the $q^0$-coefficient of the expansion of $b$ is the image of some element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\varpi\in A$ be irreducible and let $Bm$ be a $B$-algebra realising the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak n$. Then $Bm$ is a regular local ring, $\dim Bm=2$, and the image of $\mathfrak n$ in $Bm$ is generated by the images of $\varpi$ and of $j^{-1}$ (`jInvChartInf A K j`).
--
--   This is the statement that the two-chart integral model attached to the modular function field of level $M$ over a mixed-characteristic discrete valuation ring is regular at the point where the cusp $\infty$ meets the special fibre, with $\varpi$ and $1/j$ a regular system of parameters; in classical terms it is the local regularity of modular curves at $\infty$ in the style of Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur. It is used in the analysis of the minimal primes of the ideal generated by $1/j$ on the pole chart, which in turn supports the integrality and reduction arguments for the full-level modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_cuspInfty.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X0
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
